# PAN SDK execution contract

- Read root AGENTS.md and STATE.md before modifying source.
- Treat PLAN.md and docs/research/Building a Sovereign Digital Nation.md as
  directional canon. Do not invent a replacement architecture.
- Preserve PAN as a production-grade monolith. Do not introduce microservices,
  distributed infrastructure, or scaffolding folders to simulate progress.
- Work at the owning implementation seam. Do not add wrappers, shims, proxies,
  alternate packages, or duplicate logic to avoid a direct integration.
- A material architecture decision requires options and evidence before selection:
  package layout, persistence semantics, protocol/service boundary, deployment,
  external communications, publication, secrets, or destructive action.
- A mechanical defect may be repaired directly when the existing contract is
  clear; run the relevant consumer path afterward.
- Never claim success from a plan, static check, old log, or unexecuted command.
  Separate pre-existing baseline failures from introduced failures.
- Preserve unrelated working-tree changes and historical evidence.
